# Phase 5 (CTRLO-WIDER-F): a code panel's label, the fence's word, holding
# the family of p5-ctrlo-wider-inline-fam (`src/tui/drawn_wider.rs`): fx and
# xfx draw it into the panel's header rule (`blocks::append_code_panel_header`,
# `transcript_blocks.zig:1221-1238@481104fd`), on the screen and on Ctrl-O.
# Two panels: the short label (U+261D U+2E3A U+1F590, U+E0002, `a` U+FE0F,
# a soft hyphen and U+FE0F) over one line of code, and four U+261D and
# `TAIL` over 110 `w`, the panel as wide as the screen allows. `wire` keeps
# every byte written (the answer ends `END-FENCE`), for a replay on libghostty-vt
# (.prd/tui-phase5/receipts/ctrlo-wider/replay_ghostty.c).
gateway p5-ctrlo-wider-fence-turns.json
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
keep
until shown Run /help for commands
type go
wait 1
key Enter
until shown END-FENCE
until gone Generating (
snap answer
wire answer
key C-o
until shown full detail
snap ctrlo
wire ctrlo
key C-o
until gone full detail
gwlog
